Translation patch: `Cow<[T]>` conversions (`RawSeq::into_owned`, `RawSeq` deserialize, `Value::deserialize_text`)

Change: `cow.into_owned()` becomes a new helper `misc::raw::cow_into_vec(cow)` (`match cow { Borrowed(s) => s.to_vec(), Owned(v) => v }`); `RawSeq::new(bytes)` with `bytes: &[u8]` becomes `RawSeq(Cow::Borrowed(bytes), PhantomData)`.
Why: `Cow::into_owned` and `From<&[T]> for Cow` are foreign bodies (externals).
Behaviour: Identical: `into_owned` for `[T]` is `to_owned()` = `to_vec()` on `Borrowed`; `From<&[T]> for Cow` is `Cow::Borrowed`, and `RawSeq::new` just wraps `into()`.

